@aspect_governance_constraints text
Use this aspect when the task has policy, safety, trust, or governance implications that should constrain context selection.
@aspect_governance_constraints:meta json
{
  "rev": 1,
  "status": "approved",
  "aspect_type": "axiological",
  "title": "Governance constraints",
  "summary": "Select KUs that define policy, safety, trust, or value-oriented constraints relevant to the request.",
  "priority": 7,
  "domains": ["runtime", "policy", "knowledge"],
  "commands": ["planning", "kb", "credibility"],
  "interpreters": ["AdvancedReasoner", "deepLLM"],
  "tags": ["policy", "safety", "trust"],
  "query_terms": ["policy", "safety", "trust", "constraint", "risk", "governance"]
}
@aspect_governance_constraints:definition text
This aspect positions KUs by the values, policies, and governance constraints they express.
@aspect_governance_constraints:inclusion text
Include KUs that constrain what the runtime should do because of policy, safety, or trust requirements.
@aspect_governance_constraints:exclusion text
Exclude neutral descriptive KUs that do not change the acceptable action boundary.
@aspect_governance_constraints:protocol text
Prefer policy assets and other KUs whose guidance should remain visible whenever the request has safety, trust, or governance implications.
@aspect_governance_constraints:role_vocabulary json
["policy constraint", "safety note", "governance warning"]
@aspect_governance_constraints:query_terms json
["policy", "safety", "trust", "constraint", "risk", "governance"]
